                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Mario Kart walked so Sonic could drive a car, turn it into a boat, become a plane, and still finish in 8th place.\n\nThis game had absolutely no business being THIS good.\n\nThe transforming tracks are genuinely creative, drifting feels fantastic, and the colorful SEGA-inspired environments still look great. Racing on land, water, and air keeps things fresh, while World Tour offers plenty of variety.\n\nUnfortunately, the higher difficulties can be absolutely merciless, some challenges feel frustratingly unfair, and the AI occasionally races like you've personally insulted its entire family.\n\nHas it aged well? Surprisingly well. The arcade handling, track design, and cartoon visuals remain excellent. Some rough edges aside, it's still one of the strongest kart racers on PC.\n\nRatings:\n\nGameplay: 9/10\n\nGraphics: 8/10\n\nTrack Design: 9.5/10\n\nReplayability: 9/10\n\nEnjoyment: 9/10\n\nOverall: 9/10 | Recommended\n\nSEGA accidentally made a kart-racing masterpiece and then acted like that was a perfectly normal Tuesday.",
